\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Performance on the same fixed internal holdout (175 patients, 56 pCR positive). Entries are mean $\pm $ sample SD of metrics computed separately for the five seed44 fold models. Probabilities are not averaged. Macro first averages T0--T2 metrics within each fold. F1 uses threshold 0.5. Fold SD is descriptive; the five models share the holdout and overlapping training sets. Paired Macro differences are in Table~\ref {tab:bootstrap}.}}{11}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:main}{{2}{11}{Performance on the same fixed internal holdout (175 patients, 56 pCR positive). Entries are mean $\pm $ sample SD of metrics computed separately for the five seed44 fold models. Probabilities are not averaged. Macro first averages T0--T2 metrics within each fold. F1 uses threshold 0.5. Fold SD is descriptive; the five models share the holdout and overlapping training sets. Paired Macro differences are in Table~\ref {tab:bootstrap}}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Discrimination of seed-44 fold models evaluated separately. (A--C) Mean ROC curves; (D--F) mean precision--recall curves. Curves are computed per fold, interpolated onto a common grid, and averaged across five folds. Shading gives conditional 95\% shared-patient-bootstrap intervals for the mean curve. Colored values summarize directly calculated per-fold AUROC or non-interpolated AP, whose means need not equal the area under the displayed mean curve. The dotted PR reference is the 0.32 positive prevalence. No probabilities are averaged between fold models.}}{11}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:discrimination}{{2}{11}{Discrimination of seed-44 fold models evaluated separately. (A--C) Mean ROC curves; (D--F) mean precision--recall curves. Curves are computed per fold, interpolated onto a common grid, and averaged across five folds. Shading gives conditional 95\% shared-patient-bootstrap intervals for the mean curve. Colored values summarize directly calculated per-fold AUROC or non-interpolated AP, whose means need not equal the area under the displayed mean curve. The dotted PR reference is the 0.32 positive prevalence. No probabilities are averaged between fold models}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Exploratory principal Macro comparisons. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests with 99,999 shared resamples. Within each draw, metrics are computed for each fold model then equally averaged; probabilities are never averaged. All $p$ values are two-sided. Holm$_9$ adjusts the nine entries here; Holm$_{90}$ is the sensitivity analysis over all principal and secondary tests. Sig. refers to Holm$_9$. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the five fixed seed44 fold models; folds are not resampled and share one holdout.}}{12}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:bootstrap}{{3}{12}{Exploratory principal Macro comparisons. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests with 99,999 shared resamples. Within each draw, metrics are computed for each fold model then equally averaged; probabilities are never averaged. All $p$ values are two-sided. Holm$_9$ adjusts the nine entries here; Holm$_{90}$ is the sensitivity analysis over all principal and secondary tests. Sig. refers to Holm$_9$. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the five fixed seed44 fold models; folds are not resampled and share one holdout}{table.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Paired differences in fold-mean metrics at T0, T1, T2, and Macro. Colors distinguish auxiliary supervision, additional forecast readout, and the complete-model contrast. Squares denote Macro estimates. Bars are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals, with every patient draw shared across folds, models, and landmarks. Metrics are computed separately within folds before averaging. Adjusted tests appear in Tables~\ref {tab:bootstrap} and~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}. The five fold models do not create independent test cohorts.}}{12}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:paired}{{3}{12}{Paired differences in fold-mean metrics at T0, T1, T2, and Macro. Colors distinguish auxiliary supervision, additional forecast readout, and the complete-model contrast. Squares denote Macro estimates. Bars are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals, with every patient draw shared across folds, models, and landmarks. Metrics are computed separately within folds before averaging. Adjusted tests appear in Tables~\ref {tab:bootstrap} and~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}. The five fold models do not create independent test cohorts}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Operating characteristics at threshold 0.5. Entries average metrics computed separately for five seed44 fold models; Macro first averages T0--T2 within each fold. No probabilities are averaged. The same 175 patients appear in every evaluation.}}{13}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:extended_operating}{{4}{13}{Operating characteristics at threshold 0.5. Entries average metrics computed separately for five seed44 fold models; Macro first averages T0--T2 within each fold. No probabilities are averaged. The same 175 patients appear in every evaluation}{table.4}{}}
