\newlabel{tab:calibration}{{5}{14}{Probability quality: five-fold metric mean $\pm $ sample fold SD for seed44. Metrics are computed separately from each model score vector; Macro averages T0--T2 within fold. Lower is better; ECE uses ten equal-width bins}{table.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Probability quality and hypothetical decision utility of separately evaluated fold models. (A--C) Reliability summaries form five equal-count probability-rank groups of 35 patients within each fold and then average the group summaries across folds; these differ from the ten equal-width bins used for ECE. (D--F) Net-benefit curves are computed per fold and averaged, with treat-all and treat-none references. Scores are not recalibrated or averaged between models. No clinical escalation or de-escalation strategy is validated.}}{14}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:calutility}{{4}{14}{Probability quality and hypothetical decision utility of separately evaluated fold models. (A--C) Reliability summaries form five equal-count probability-rank groups of 35 patients within each fold and then average the group summaries across folds; these differ from the ten equal-width bins used for ECE. (D--F) Net-benefit curves are computed per fold and averaged, with treat-all and treat-none references. Scores are not recalibrated or averaged between models. No clinical escalation or de-escalation strategy is validated}{figure.4}{}}
