\newlabel{tab:foldresults}{{A.7}{20}{Individual seed44 fold-model results for direct readouts. Each fold model is evaluated separately on the same 175 patients (56 positive), without averaging probabilities. Macro averages the three landmark metrics. The folds are overlapping training partitions, not independent test cohorts}{table.7}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.8}{\ignorespaces Individual seed44 fold-model results for forecast readouts. Evaluation and aggregation match Table~\ref {tab:foldresults}; these individual fold metrics generate the mean and sample SD in the main tables.}}{21}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:foldresults_forecast}{{A.8}{21}{Individual seed44 fold-model results for forecast readouts. Evaluation and aggregation match Table~\ref {tab:foldresults}; these individual fold metrics generate the mean and sample SD in the main tables}{table.8}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.9}{\ignorespaces All 14 macro metrics for the principal variants: point estimate [95\% patient-bootstrap percentile interval]. Metrics are computed separately for each seed44 fold model, averaged over T0--T2 within fold, then equally averaged over five folds. Probabilities are not averaged. Threshold-dependent metrics use 0.5. Identical patient resamples preserve pairing across models and landmarks. Entries are marginal model intervals; paired differences are reported separately. Intervals condition on the fitted fold models and exclude retraining and retrospective selection uncertainty. Downward arrows identify metrics for which lower is better.}}{22}{table.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:extended_macro}{{A.9}{22}{All 14 macro metrics for the principal variants: point estimate [95\% patient-bootstrap percentile interval]. Metrics are computed separately for each seed44 fold model, averaged over T0--T2 within fold, then equally averaged over five folds. Probabilities are not averaged. Threshold-dependent metrics use 0.5. Identical patient resamples preserve pairing across models and landmarks. Entries are marginal model intervals; paired differences are reported separately. Intervals condition on the fitted fold models and exclude retraining and retrospective selection uncertainty. Downward arrows identify metrics for which lower is better}{table.9}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.10}{\ignorespaces Threshold sensitivity analysis: seed44 five-fold metric means. Each fold model uses its own landmark-specific validation Youden threshold on the holdout scores from the same model. Validation also informed best-checkpoint selection; this is sensitivity analysis, not nested calibration. No test labels choose thresholds.}}{22}{table.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:extended_threshold}{{A.10}{22}{Threshold sensitivity analysis: seed44 five-fold metric means. Each fold model uses its own landmark-specific validation Youden threshold on the holdout scores from the same model. Validation also informed best-checkpoint selection; this is sensitivity analysis, not nested calibration. No test labels choose thresholds}{table.10}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.11}{\ignorespaces Exploratory landmark comparisons. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across folds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the five fixed seed44 fold models; folds are not resampled and share one holdout.}}{23}{table.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:significance_landmarks}{{A.11}{23}{Exploratory landmark comparisons. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across folds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the five fixed seed44 fold models; folds are not resampled and share one holdout}{table.11}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.12}{\ignorespaces Exploratory Macro operating and probability-quality comparisons. Differences are first-named minus second-named model; negative Brier, NLL, or ECE differences favor the first model. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across folds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the five fixed seed44 fold models; folds are not resampled and share one holdout.}}{24}{table.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:significance_extended}{{A.12}{24}{Exploratory Macro operating and probability-quality comparisons. Differences are first-named minus second-named model; negative Brier, NLL, or ECE differences favor the first model. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across folds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the five fixed seed44 fold models; folds are not resampled and share one holdout}{table.12}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.13}{\ignorespaces Exploratory pooling comparisons: ForecastAttention minus ForecastMean. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across folds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the five fixed seed44 fold models; folds are not resampled and share one holdout.}}{24}{table.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:significance_pooling}{{A.13}{24}{Exploratory pooling comparisons: ForecastAttention minus ForecastMean. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across folds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the five fixed seed44 fold models; folds are not resampled and share one holdout}{table.13}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.14}{\ignorespaces Exploratory paired T2 minus T0 comparisons. Shared patient-bootstrap draws retain dependence between folds and landmarks. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across folds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the five fixed seed44 fold models; folds are not resampled and share one holdout.}}{25}{table.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:significance_longitudinal}{{A.14}{25}{Exploratory paired T2 minus T0 comparisons. Shared patient-bootstrap draws retain dependence between folds and landmarks. All metrics use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests (99,999 shared draws across folds, models, and landmarks). All $p$ values are two-sided. $p_{\mathrm {Holm}}$ adjusts jointly over the 81 secondary tests in Tables~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}--\ref {tab:significance_longitudinal}. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the five fixed seed44 fold models; folds are not resampled and share one holdout}{table.14}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A.8}{\ignorespaces Outcome-conditioned changes in predicted pCR probability from T0 to T2. Each fold model supplies one probability change per patient. Histograms are constructed separately within folds and then equally averaged; probabilities are not averaged between models. Panels separate variants and outcome classes. Repeated fold predictions are correlated observations of the same 175 patients and do not multiply the sample size by five. Score changes do not establish individual treatment effects.}}{25}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:scorechanges}{{A.8}{25}{Outcome-conditioned changes in predicted pCR probability from T0 to T2. Each fold model supplies one probability change per patient. Histograms are constructed separately within folds and then equally averaged; probabilities are not averaged between models. Panels separate variants and outcome classes. Repeated fold predictions are correlated observations of the same 175 patients and do not multiply the sample size by five. Score changes do not establish individual treatment effects}{figure.8}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {B.15}{\ignorespaces Exploratory subgroup discrimination using seed 44, with each fold model evaluated separately. Model entries are means $\pm $ sample SD of five independently calculated fold metrics; Macro first averages T0--T2 within each fold. No prediction probabilities are averaged. Paired patient-bootstrap intervals for the mean ForecastAttention minus NoJEPA difference condition on the five fixed fold models. Age 50 is an exploratory reporting cutpoint. Namespace groups are parts of one clinical release, not external cohorts.}}{26}{table.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:subgroups}{{B.15}{26}{Exploratory subgroup discrimination using seed 44, with each fold model evaluated separately. Model entries are means $\pm $ sample SD of five independently calculated fold metrics; Macro first averages T0--T2 within each fold. No prediction probabilities are averaged. Paired patient-bootstrap intervals for the mean ForecastAttention minus NoJEPA difference condition on the five fixed fold models. Age 50 is an exploratory reporting cutpoint. Namespace groups are parts of one clinical release, not external cohorts}{table.15}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {B.16}{\ignorespaces Archived seed44 epoch 20 fixed-training-probe diagnostics, shown as mean $\pm $ descriptive sample SD across five fold-specific statistics. Skill is $1-\mathrm  {L1}_{forecast}/\mathrm  {L1}_{copy}$ within each snapshot\textquotesingle s EMA coordinates; positive is better than holding the landmark state constant. Forecast targets require a continuous actually observed visit chain. These are training-probe summaries, not best-checkpoint holdout forecast evaluations. NoJEPA has no trained-world diagnostic.}}{26}{table.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:worldprobe}{{B.16}{26}{Archived seed44 epoch 20 fixed-training-probe diagnostics, shown as mean $\pm $ descriptive sample SD across five fold-specific statistics. Skill is $1-\mathrm {L1}_{forecast}/\mathrm {L1}_{copy}$ within each snapshot\textquotesingle s EMA coordinates; positive is better than holding the landmark state constant. Forecast targets require a continuous actually observed visit chain. These are training-probe summaries, not best-checkpoint holdout forecast evaluations. NoJEPA has no trained-world diagnostic}{table.16}{}}
